      "worked": "Equate the curves.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx^2&=k-(x-k)^2\\\\\n2x^2-2kx+k^2-k&=0.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor tangency, the intersection equation has a repeated root, so $\\Delta=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n(-2k)^2-4(2)(k^2-k)&=0\\\\\n4k^2-8(k^2-k)&=0\\\\\n4k(2-k)&=0\\\\\nk&=0\\text{ or }2.\n\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $k=0$, the intersection equation is $2x^2=0$, giving the point $(0,0)$. When $k=2$, it is $2(x-1)^2=0$, giving the point $(1,1)$. Each case has a repeated root, so both values are valid.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
